From: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: add a parameter to refuse A-MSDUs in A-MPDUs

mac80211 splits every received A-MSDU into one skb per subframe. With
paged RX buffers the subframes reference page fragments, and on a host
whose Ethernet driver cannot scatter-gather they are linearized again
before they can be forwarded; copying them into linear skbs right away
costs the same. On the EN751221 (one MIPS 34Kc core) that copy took 27 %
of the CPU at 300 Mbit/s of Wi-Fi upload.

Add mt76_rx_amsdu_in_ampdu (default on). When cleared, mt76 does not set
SUPPORTS_AMSDU_IN_AMPDU, so ADDBA responses tell stations not to put
A-MSDUs into A-MPDUs and every MPDU arrives in a linear buffer.

Signed-off-by: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@
 	.max_power = 30,			\
 }
 
+/* let stations put A-MSDUs into A-MPDUs (advertised in ADDBA responses) */
+static bool mt76_rx_amsdu_in_ampdu = true;
+module_param(mt76_rx_amsdu_in_ampdu, bool, 0444);
+
 static const struct ieee80211_channel mt76_channels_2ghz[] = {
 	CHAN2G(1, 2412),
 	CHAN2G(2, 2417),
@@ -476,7 +480,8 @@
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_RC_TABLE);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORT_FAST_XMIT);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_CLONED_SKBS);
-	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_AMSDU_IN_AMPDU);
+	if (mt76_rx_amsdu_in_ampdu)
+		ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_AMSDU_IN_AMPDU);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_REORDERING_BUFFER);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SPECTRUM_MGMT);
 
